# empirical-software-engineering

Apply the empirical-software-engineering skill when the request matches its scope.

Capabilities:
- operationalize software-engineering constructs and estimands
- design experiments, quasi-experiments, case studies, surveys, and mining-software-repositories studies
- assess causal threats, selection, measurement, missingness, privacy, and ethics
- produce a provenance-aware empirical study artifact and decision report

Stop when: Constructs and estimands are operationalized; design and identification assumptions are explicit; provenance, analysis plan, uncertainty, validity threats, ethics/privacy, and decision boundaries are documented; unsupported causal claims are downgraded or blocked.
